# These documentation assets used to be tracked with git-LFS to keep the
# repository lightweight. That broke the published site: the GitLab ->
# GitHub push mirror (github.com/ngsxfem/ngsxditto, source for GitHub Pages
# at ngsxfem.github.io/ngsxditto/) does not transfer LFS binary objects --
# only the small pointer files -- so GitHub's LFS store never had the real
# content, and the deployed site served raw "version
# https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1 ..." pointer text as if it were the
# image/gif/html file. At ~4.5 MB total these assets are small enough that
# storing them as ordinary git blobs (which the mirror *does* replicate
# correctly) is simpler and more robust than fixing LFS mirroring.
